        { "id": 5, "text": "The expression inside the square root, b² - 4ac, is so important it has its own name: the discriminant. It 'discriminates' or tells us how many real solutions we'll have.", "duration": 13 },
        { "id": 6, "text": "If it's positive, we get two real solutions. If it's zero, we get one real solution. And if it's negative, we get no real solutions, because you can't take the square root of a negative number in the real number system.", "duration": 14 },
        { "id": 7, "text": "Finally, the whole thing is divided by 2a. To use it, you just need to identify a, b, and c from your equation and carefully plug them into the formula.", "duration": 9 }
